WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.403
- Before we say goodbye,
y'all, I have one last story

00:00:02.403 --> 00:00:05.787
from the world of social
media, this is What I'm Liking.

00:00:05.787 --> 00:00:07.597
(audience cheering)

00:00:07.597 --> 00:00:10.980
November is National
Family Caregivers Month,

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:14.430
which recognizes the 53
million people who provide care

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:16.770
to an elderly or disabled loved one.

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:19.260
It's stressful and often isolating work,

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:21.510
something author, Debbie
Weiss, can relate to.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:24.480
For over 40 years, she
cared for her father,

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.090
then her son, and finally her husband.

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:29.010
It's a story she shares in her new book,

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:31.080
On Second Thought...Maybe I Can.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.610
Let's get Debbie in here, everybody.

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:33.869
Give it up for Debbie.

00:00:33.869 --> 00:00:35.853
(audience cheering)

00:00:35.853 --> 00:00:36.686
Hi Debbie.

00:00:37.592 --> 00:00:38.490
- Hi Kelly.

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:41.190
- Well, thank you for joining
us and, and I just have to say

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:44.460
you're, you've been a caregiver
your whole life, right?

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.050
- My whole life, you said it.

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:47.100
40 years.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:50.520
I was thrust into
caregiving when I was 17,

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:53.640
when my father, at 46,
had a massive stroke,

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.010
became permanently disabled,

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:59.310
and soon afterwards, my parents divorced

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:03.390
and I became his primary
caregiver for the next 30 years

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:05.400
and then when my oldest son was two,

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.710
he was diagnosed on the autistic spectrum

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:11.070
and added anxiety and
depression a little later on

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.170
and more recently, about five years ago,

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:16.200
my husband became permanently disabled

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:19.650
and unfortunately passed
away on December 30th.

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:20.483
- [Kelly] Oh God.

00:01:20.483 --> 00:01:24.510
- And I've spent the majority
of my life caring for others

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:27.240
and after many years,

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:31.710
I was exhausted, angry,
resentful, and bitter

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:35.790
and I hate to admit it,
but I felt sorry for myself

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:40.790
and I then realized that
I was feeling this way

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:44.759
because I neglected myself
for all those years and-

00:01:44.759 --> 00:01:45.592
- [Kelly] Absolutely.

00:01:45.592 --> 00:01:48.630
- That realization was a
big game changer for me.

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:49.463
- [Kelly] Yeah,

00:01:49.463 --> 00:01:52.020
so that change then
created this book, right?

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:55.110
- [Debbie] It has been a long
journey over the last 10 years

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:57.360
that actually led to the book, yes.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:58.470
- Absolutely.

00:01:58.470 --> 00:01:59.910
What do you hope people,
when they read it,

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:01.290
what do you hope they get out of it?

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:02.123
- [Debbie] Oh, goodness.

00:02:02.123 --> 00:02:06.390
Well, I hope they learn
what I eventually did,

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:11.250
that prioritizing your
own care is not selfish.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.920
It's a necessity and when we do that,

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:17.820
we actually show up as better caregivers

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:22.230
and just better people for
everyone else in our lives.

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:24.090
You know, we don't really have to choose

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:26.670
between ourselves and our loved ones.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:30.060
We all have the capacity to care for both.

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:30.893
- [Kelly] Absolutely.

00:02:30.893 --> 00:02:33.210
The, I would say it's
the oxygen mask mentality

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:34.410
when you're on the airplane.

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:36.180
You know, they always tell
you, okay, put yours on first

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:37.710
and then help, you know, your little ones

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:39.570
and that's hard to implement in life,

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:41.460
especially if you've
grown up with, you know,

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.050
being told like, have a servant's heart,

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:44.040
always look out for others

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:45.360
and you always put yourself aside.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:46.860
It's kind of how I grew up as well,

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:49.260
and it's hard to change, to pivot that.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:50.340
Thank you so much, Debbie.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:51.937
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:51.937 --> 00:02:54.313
(audience cheering)

00:02:54.313 --> 00:02:56.220
And that's not all, ma'am.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:58.920
Our season long partner,
Pilot pen, makers of FriXion,

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:01.110
the go-to race erasable pen
of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:02.970
love your support for caregivers.

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:04.320
So on your behalf,

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:06.750
they're writing Family
Caregivers Alliance a check

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:08.580
for a thousand dollars.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:09.990
For more than 40 years,

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:12.720
this organization has
provided services and support

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:14.700
for caregivers like yourself,

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.340
so thank you so much for
putting 'em on everybody's radar

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:18.486
to pay attention to.

00:03:18.486 --> 00:03:19.500
(audience cheering)

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:21.600
Thank you, Debbie.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:24.180
Before we go, I wanna remind you to watch

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:26.910
the 91st Christmas in Rockefeller Center

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:28.380
tomorrow night at 8:00.

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:30.330
I am hosting and will also be performing

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:32.850
alongside a star studded lineup.

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:35.460
It airs on NBC and Peacock,
so be sure to check it out.

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:36.690
It's gonna be incredible.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:38.280
Thanks to all our guests
this hour, everybody.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:42.660
Mark Harmon, Kel Mitchell,
Aaron, Zach, and Lanita

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:43.710
and Debbie, of course.

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:46.583
Y'all have a great day and if
it's not, try and change it.

